n of the whole is shaded?"}, {"do": "show", "target": ["s1", "s2", "s3", "s4", "s5"], "at": "shaded"}]}, {"speaker": "learner", "say": "Five fourths! Five parts are shaded, and four are not.", "pause": 0.05, "do": [{"do": "show", "target": "e1", "at": "Five", "nth": 2}, {"do": "write", "tex": "\\dfrac{5}{4}", "id": "guess", "at": "fourths"}, {"do": "show", "target": "e2", "at": "four"}]}, {"speaker": "teacher", "say": "Hmm. Five and four are real counts, but they are not the right two. Two counts, in the right order, will always work.", "pause": 0.4, "do": [{"do": "highlight", "target": "e1", "at": "Five", "until": "and"}, {"do": "highlight", "target": "e2", "at": "four", "until": "are"}, {"do": "strike", "target": "guess", "at": "not"}, {"do": "hide", "target": ["e1", "e2"], "at": "not"}, {"do": "text", "text": "Two counts, in the right order", "at": "Two", "nth": 2}]}, {"speaker": "teacher", "say": "First, count every equal part, shaded or not: one, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine.", "pause": 0.3, "do": [{"do": "text", "text": "First: count every equal part", "at": "First"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p1", "at": "one"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p2", "at": "two"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p3", "at": "three"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p4", "at": "four"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p5", "at": "five"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p6", "at": "six"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p7", "at": "seven"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p8", "at": "eight"}, {"do": "show", "target": "p9", "at": "nine"}]}, {"speaker": "teacher", "say": "Nine equal parts. The bottom number is nine. It names the piece: one ninth.", "pause": 0.4, "do": [{"do": "term", "word": "denominator", "meaning": "the bottom number: how many equal parts", "at": "bottom"}, {"do": "show", "target": "n0", "at": "ninth"}]}, {"speaker": "teacher", "say": "Now watch the top number. I will take the shading away, and put it back one piece at a time.", "pause": 0.4, "do": [{"do": "hide", "target": ["s1", "s2", "